From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: builder <builder@esp32-repro>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:09:08 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] video: fbdev: add a Quad-SPI AMOLED (SH8601/CO5300)
 driver

Framebuffer in RAM, dirty-rectangle updates through a delayed work, register
writes on one line and pixels on four (or one, as a fallback). Supports the
CO5300 and SH8601 init sequences of the Waveshare 1.43" panel, a brightness
attribute, and refresh/reinit/cmd/flush_stats attributes for bring-up.
---
 drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig          |  13 +
 drivers/video/fbdev/Makefile         |   1 +
 drivers/video/fbdev/amoled-qspi-fb.c | 853 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 867 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/video/fbdev/amoled-qspi-fb.c

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig b/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig
index 085d3a202..a299f4fa1 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/Kconfig
@@ -1787,6 +1787,19 @@ config FB_SSD1307
 	  This driver implements support for the Solomon SSD1307
 	  OLED controller over I2C.
 
+config FB_AMOLED_QSPI
+	tristate "Quad-SPI AMOLED (SH8601/CO5300) framebuffer support"
+	depends on FB && SPI && GPIOLIB
+	select FB_SYSMEM_HELPERS
+	help
+	  Framebuffer driver for AMOLED panels with an SH8601 or CO5300
+	  controller on a Quad-SPI bus, such as the 466x466 panel of the
+	  Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-AMOLED-1.43.
+
+	  The framebuffer is kept in RAM and the parts that change are sent
